# In the Hall of the Mountain King
# Composer: Edvard Grieg (1843-1907). Work: Peer Gynt Suite No. 1, Op. 46, No. 4 (1874-75), public domain.
# Arrangement: ours, for four chip voices, 2026-10-25. Notes written from Grieg's own piano score (The University
# Society, 1918; public-domain edition typeset by the Mutopia Project, piece 1888): melody, the pizzicato bass and the
# off-beat chords. Shortened (each phrase pair once per tempo step) and the octave doublings are our choices.
# The accelerando: the score starts at quarter = 138 and speeds up to the end ("sempre stretto sin al fine");
# here every bar is a little faster, from quarter = 120 to 200, which keeps the staccato notes clear on a small
# speaker; the closing hits stay at 200.
# One row is a sixteenth note, so each tempo value is twice the quarter-note BPM.
# Columns: lead (pulse 25%) | harmony (pulse 50%) | bass (triangle) | drums (noise). Tokens as in fox_run.tune.
vol 11 7 13 7
# intro: the fermata F# octave in the low strings
tempo 240
